  "prefLabel": "Plu 203.03 Right to A Hearing",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plu 203.03 Right to A Hearing. Any person having a dispute with the board shall be entitled to a hearing of the dispute if:\n\n(a) The legal rights, duties or privileges of that person will be determined in the course of deciding the outcome of the dispute; and\n\n(b) Constitutional, statutory or case law requires the board to hold a hearing before determination of those rights, duties or privileges.\n\nSource. #8464, eff 10-28-05",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plu100-500.html"
